% CASE · Signal — the fast, tech-feeling cue (27 s, 128 bpm, E minor): every move of rhythm.md in notation.
% Measured section loudness: hook −16.5 · verse −18.6 · build −16.1 · stop −21.2 · drop −13.9 dB RMS —
% steps up, a stop, then the peak. (A first draft opened at the same level as the drop; the hook was
% taken down one dynamic so the drop has somewhere to go.)
% bars 1–2  hook hot: four-on-the-floor, hats, bass and the pluck figure from the first beat, a crash, mf.
% bars 3–6  half-time verse: the snare only on beat 3 — the feel changes, the tempo does not; the
%           bass in a 3+3+2; bar 6 ends with a !stutter! turnaround.
% bars 7–8  build: the whole mix filtered open (!filter!), snare eighths then sixteenths, a tape stop
%           (!stop!) on the last beat.
% bar 9     the stop: half a bar of silence with only a riser pulling into the drop.
% bars 10–13 drop (!hit! = impact + subdrop): kick on every beat, off-beat supersaw stabs, violins sing
%           the hook in octaves, piano octaves on the downbeats, sixteenth plucks.
% bar 14    button: one hit together, then nothing; the crash rings out.
